WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.675
Practical IEC 62443 adoption begins with scope and ownership.

00:00:04.675 --> 00:00:08.510
Define the system under consideration, the physical process it supports,

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:11.815
responsible organizations, lifecycle stage, and risk decision makers.

00:00:11.815 --> 00:00:16.470
Build an asset inventory that includes devices, software, firmware, communication paths,

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:19.360
remote connections, suppliers, and operational dependencies.

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:22.000
Perform risk assessment with engineers and operators.

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:26.600
Identify credible threats, vulnerabilities, existing safeguards, process consequences,

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:27.840
and required recovery.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.305
Use the results to define zones, conduits, target security levels, and requirements.

00:00:32.305 --> 00:00:36.080
Avoid copying an architecture from another site without confirming that functions and

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:37.100
consequences match.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:41.155
Review the architecture for unnecessary connectivity and uncontrolled trust.

00:00:41.155 --> 00:00:45.540
Design segmentation, secure remote access, administration, monitoring, backups,

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:47.076
and update pathways together.

00:00:47.076 --> 00:00:50.920
Procurement and supplier requirements should state expected capabilities, evidence,

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.155
vulnerability handling, support periods, and integration assumptions.

00:00:54.155 --> 00:00:58.480
During implementation, configure component security features, remove unused functions,

00:00:58.480 --> 00:01:01.285
manage identities and privileges, document exceptions,

00:01:01.285 --> 00:01:03.600
and test controls under realistic conditions.

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:07.635
Acceptance testing should verify security behavior as well as process operation.

00:01:07.635 --> 00:01:11.840
The asset owner needs accurate diagrams, account ownership, configuration records,

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.325
backup procedures, and recovery information.

00:01:14.325 --> 00:01:18.005
Operation requires change control, vulnerability management, monitoring,

00:01:18.005 --> 00:01:22.320
incident response, periodic access review, backup testing, and lifecycle planning.

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.660
Evidence should show what was implemented, who approved it, how it was tested,

00:01:25.660 --> 00:01:27.195
and how deviations are managed.

00:01:27.195 --> 00:01:30.910
Metrics should support decisions rather than exist only for reporting.

00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:33.430
Organizations do not need to solve every issue at once.

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:37.435
Start with high-consequence systems and pathways, create achievable improvement plans,

00:01:37.435 --> 00:01:41.255
and integrate cybersecurity with existing engineering, safety, reliability,

00:01:41.255 --> 00:01:42.480
and maintenance processes.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:47.900
IEC 62443 works best as an operating discipline, not a one-time documentation project.
